// @run
// @log 0
// THE PRICE OF DROPPING `W` FROM D301's LANDING (silent-class-inventory D301).
//
// D300's kind-1 rung is ref-list slot EQUALITY. This program's two map-value slots hold
// DIFFERENT rl slots (0 and 2) that resolve the SAME wrapper (8), because `Circle` and
// `CircleN` are two declared names of one layout and intern two `rlInternName` rows which
// `rlTwin` then merges. Slot equality cannot see that; `repStructSlotsTwin` over the two
// rows' element struct rows can, timing-independently.
//
// WHY THIS IS A NAMED CELL AND NOT A DERIVED ONE. The census's `twin` axis crosses
// declaration twins and its `cont` axis picks ONE container per cell, so no census
// coordinate carries a SECOND declared layout twin beside a nested container — measured,
// the whole 1,477-class derived corpus moves 0 cells under `W` in either direction, and so
// do all 1,913 buildable corpus modules (`cmp`, byte-identical). Only this program moves.
//
// Grades, all measured: master (R+X+T) check-clean invalid wasm; `W` alone still
// check-clean invalid wasm; `X` alone still check-clean invalid wasm; `W+X` runs. The two
// hoists are ONE landing at this shape, exactly as they were at D300's.
type Circle = { r: i32 | null }
type CircleN = { r: i32 | null }
const iv = Map()
iv["k0"] = { r: null }
const om = Map()
om["k0"] = iv
const dd: {[string]: {[string]: CircleN}} = om
print(dd.size - 1)
